{
  "title": "105: al-Feel الفيل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِاَصْحٰبِ الْفِيْلِؕ‏(1)\nALAM TARA KAYFA FA-A’LA RABBOKA BE-ASHAABIL FEEL.\nWhat! Hast thou not seen how thy Lord dealt with the fellows of the Elephant?\nاَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِىْ تَضْلِيْلٍۙ‏(2)\nALAM YAJ-A’L KAYDAHUM FEE TAZLEELINW.\nDidst He not cause their device to err\nوَّاَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا اَبَابِيْلَۙ‏(3)\nWA ARSALA A’LAYHIM TAYRAN ABAABEELA.\nAnd sent He down upon them birds in flocks\nتَرْمِيْهِمْ بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍۙ‏(4)\nTARMEEHIM BE-HEJAARATIM MIN SIJJEELIN.\nPelting them with stones of baked clay\nفَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّاْكُوْلٍ‏(5)\nFA-JA-A’LAHUM KA-A’SFIM MAAKOOL.\nThus rendered them like straw, eaten up (by cattle)?",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah with 5 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah in his obligatory prayers, the mountains will bear witness on the Day of Judgement that he prayed and he will be taken to Paradise on the command of Allah (s.w.t.).\nThe person who recites this Surah is kept safe from his enemies and has his difficulties and problems solved quickly. Recitation of this Surah is also helpful in remaining safe from evil tyrant rulers."
